                "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 22 at 2:57AM AKST until November 23 at 3:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Elevated coastal water levels of 1 to 2 feet above the\nnormal highest tide line.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal Kuskokwim Delta Communities, including Kipnuk,\nKongiganak, and Kwigillingok.\n\n* WHEN...3 AM Sunday to 3 AM AKST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Elevated coastal water levels driven by southeast\nwinds gusting to 55 mph. Coastal erosion is possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Gusty southeasterly winds will begin\nincreasing early Sunday morning as the storm approaches.\nHighest water levels expected late Sunday night. Winds will\ndiminish by Sunday evening, and seas will subside by Monday\nmorning following the natural high tide cycle.",
